notes.body:
> All other protocols need to be checked also.

Most protocols use `find_conversation_pinfo()` (or `find_or_create_conversation()` which calls that), which updates `last_frame`. When you switch to using `find_conversation` directly, you become responsible for updating `last_frame`.

In practice, in TCP there are a number other other calls to `find_conversation_pinfo()` or `find_or_create_conversation()` so that it eventually gets set correctly, but it should be set ( as soon as you've definitely decided on which conversation you're using. (So line 7231.)

```
if (pinfo->num > conv->last_frame) {
    conv->last_frame = pinfo->num;
}
```

